CommitDate: Sat Jun 20 11:05:07 2026 -0400

    fix: correct canonical boundary operator + regenerate all results out-of-sample
    
    generate_thesis_artifacts.first_zero_crossing (imported by cross_family) and
    frontier_validation_report.first_zero_crossing had the same defect as the
    trace_analysis copy: no t>=2 floor + step-1 fallback -> theory-forbidden step-1
    boundaries. Now T* = inf{t>=2: drift<=0}, None if never observed.
    
    Regenerated every cell (re-graded labels + out-of-sample analysis) and the
    cross-family report. Net effect of the full remediation:
    - boundaries: theory-forbidden step-1s gone (weak models now 2); late witnesses
      unchanged (Qwen 7/14/32 = 5); capability ladder and cross-family conclusion intact.
    - probe AUC now honest out-of-fold: max 0.91 (Qwen-14B) vs inflated in-sample 0.96;
      most models 0.65-0.75.
    - 545/165000 labels corrected by the re-grade.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/research/frontier_validation_report.py b/research/frontier_validation_report.py
index b56c8c5..a598333 100644
--- a/research/frontier_validation_report.py
+++ b/research/frontier_validation_report.py
@@ -116,18 +116,14 @@ def relative_gain_pct(current: float, baseline: float) -> float:
     return 100.0 * (current - baseline) / baseline
 
 
-def first_zero_crossing(frame: pd.DataFrame, column: str) -> int | None:
+def first_zero_crossing(frame: pd.DataFrame, column: str, t_min: int = 2) -> int | None:
+    # AUDIT FIX: T* = inf{t >= t_min : col(t) <= 0}; None if never observed. The
+    # previous version had no t_min floor and a step-1 fallback (theory-forbidden).
     valid = frame.dropna(subset=[column]).sort_values("step")
-    if valid.empty:
-        return None
-    previous = None
-    for _, row in valid.iterrows():
-        value = float(row[column])
-        if previous is not None and previous > 0.0 and value <= 0.0:
-            return int(row["step"])
-        previous = value
-    if float(valid.iloc[0][column]) <= 0.0:
-        return int(valid.iloc[0]["step"])
+    eligible = valid[valid["step"] >= t_min]
+    crossed = eligible[eligible[column] <= 0.0]
+    if len(crossed):
+        return int(crossed.iloc[0]["step"])
     return None
 
 
